            ; ── 857 ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
            ; Stone 17 put GGUF type 40 (MXFP4) on the GPU and expected to have
            ; to BUY the accumulation's honesty. Stone 13 had to: hoisting Q6_K's
            ; d*sc out of the slot sum changed the per-term rounding, so
            ; qk-matvec-slot.fk derived an epsilon and the carrier measures the
            ; realised deviation against it every run. The same hoist here looked
            ; like the same debt.
            ; It was not a debt. It was a GRANT, and the coarseness of the format
            ; made it. The MX scale is an exact power of two, so (s*v)*x and
            ; s*(v*x) are the same f32 term by term and the hoist costs nothing.
            ; Then the same coarseness paid again, one level up: every E2M1 value
            ; is a multiple of 0.5 and this tensor's exponents are 2^-7..2^-5, so
            ; every weight is a multiple of 2^-8, every product a multiple of
            ; 2^-16, and every partial sum stays on that lattice, bounded far
            ; below 2^8. A multiple of 2^-16 under 2^8 needs at most 24
            ; significand bits — exactly what f32 has. So a 4096-term f32 dot
            ; product came back EQUAL to Form's fp64 answer, bit for bit, with
            ; no rounding anywhere to disagree about.
            ; The instinct trained by every wider format is that coarse data
            ; costs precision and must be compensated. Sometimes it GRANTS
            ; precision instead: the lattice is coarse enough that the arithmetic
            ; downstream cannot leave it, and the error budget was never spent
            ; because there was nothing to spend it on.
            ; The discipline this asks for is not celebration but suspicion in
            ; the right direction: an exactly-zero deviation reads identically to
            ; a stalled kernel writing zeros, so the gate that reports it must
            ; also refuse a zero denominator and print the values. Ours did not,
            ; at first; the MXFP8 rows in the same run, which DO show the ordinary
            ; f32/fp64 gap, are what turned the zero from a worry into a witness.
            ; Distinct from what the body carries: selfgauge 834 names a ratio's
            ; denominator, and here the denominator was fine while the NUMERATOR
