            ; there was nothing there to collapse. The whole token is already ONE
            ; command buffer, one concurrent encoder; the 113 us lived only inside
            ; FORM_PROFILE, which commits and waits after each op to attribute it —
            ; and THAT commit+wait IS the 113 us. The profiler priced its own cut.
            ; A non-perturbing instrument settled it: duplicate an op IN STREAM,
            ; inside the same command buffer, and divide the whole-token delta by
            ; the count. 896 extra barriered dispatches per token (dispatches
            ; 425 -> 1321), whether 1-element adds or 8192-element SwiGLUs, did not
            ; move decode at all. The one duplication that costs is re-reading a
            ; ~20 MB weight tensor: the FFN up-projection dup added 66 %. So the
            ; wall is WEIGHT MEMORY BANDWIDTH — the ~196 matvecs stream the ~2 GB
            ; quantised model once per token, ~68 GB/s cold on this chip; ollama's
            ; 6.34 ms/token is the same 2 GB nearer the ceiling. The seam was never
            ; 86 % of the token; it was ~0 % of it, and 100 % of the profiler.
