            ; row 876 buildbound (2026-07-22, Stone 40): giving the body an O(1)
            ; keyed map began by writing the textbook shape — hash, an array of B
            ; buckets, a short in-bucket scan — and the body refused it, for a
            ; reason that has nothing to do with lookup. On the Go kernel a Form
            ; list is a Go slice: nth indexes it and tail reslices it, both O(1),
            ; but cons COPIES, so constructing any list of length L costs O(L^2)
            ; (measured, warm, one process, one clock: 20 000 by cons = 1948 ms,
            ; 40 000 = 8953 ms — 4.6x for 2x). A flat B-bucket table therefore
            ; costs O(B^2) to rebuild on every insert: quadratic in the very
            ; number that must grow for the lookup to stay flat. The shape that
            ; makes the query O(1) is the shape the body cannot build. What
            ; worked was a 16-ary trie, whose node is sixteen cells WHATEVER the
            ; map holds — path-copying an insert rebuilds depth lists of sixteen,
            ; a constant, while the bucket count is 16^depth. The trie is not
            ; there because it is elegant; it is there because on a kernel whose
            ; only aggregate constructor copies, the buildable structures are
            ; exactly those whose node size does not depend on n. The write
            ; primitive chose the read structure. This is equireach (row 822) one
            ; step over: equireach names what a door costs to READ, buildbound
            ; names what a constructor costs you in SHAPE — and unlike a reach
            ; cost, which arrives as a slow answer, this one arrives as a design
            ; that is simply unreachable, so no benchmark can see it and only
            ; whoever tries to build the thing ever meets it. "buildbound" —
            ; 0 hits across learn/, receipts/, docs/, teachings/, form/ before
            ; this row (instrument validated on the same command: gapghost 9,
            ; thawtax 7 — a grep of nothing is a claim about the instrument
            ; until a control makes it hit).
