            ; 929 — tickblind. Building the gender cell, a mutation was restored and
            ; the band still read the MUTATED verdict while the source plainly read
            ; the original. Clearing the .fkb gave the right answer. Controlled:
            ;   without an mtime bump   7 of 8 mutate/restore cycles served a STALE image
            ;   with an mtime bump      0 of 6
            ; .fkb freshness is mtime-based at one-second granularity, so a tight
            ; edit-run-edit-run loop lands the source write and the cache write in the
            ; same tick and the edit is never seen. The bump fixing it completely is
            ; what confirms the mechanism instead of guessing at it.
            ; The failure direction is the bad one: mutated=511, the band reporting the
            ; previous GREEN verdict on mutated source. And the workload that triggers
            ; it is MUTATION TESTING — this body's central verification discipline.
            ; Every mutation table in every receipt here was produced by that loop.
            ; So: a cache keyed on WHEN a file changed cannot tell two changes apart
            ; inside one tick, and the faster you verify the blinder it gets. The
            ; defect scales WITH diligence — a slow reviewer never meets it; eight
            ; mutations in ten seconds meets it seven times.
