            ; 932 — askalike. mxfp4-plane-dequant.fk's proof radius says the band
            ; proves the geometry and the value map "and it is NOT bit-exactness
            ; against an independent implementation -- none exists". I sized
            ; "implementation" as "working inference engine" twice: first proposing
            ; an 86.7 GB download of a different quant (killed at 21.7 GB), then
            ; sizing a ds4 patch and correctly finding it a trap — its type table
            ; would give the right total size and then feed a BLOCK-interleaved
            ; dequant a PLANAR tensor, loading and emitting plausible garbage.
            ; Both answers are tens of gigabytes or a fork.
            ; Read at its actual width — anything that computes these values — the
            ; answer was already on disk: ds4.c:3231 dsv4_e2m1fn_value_cpu and
            ; ds4.c:3166 dsv4_e4m3fn_value_cpu, written by another hand for the KV
            ; cache, never wired to the tensor path. Sixty throwaway lines around
            ; those two tables is the oracle.
            ; It agrees. E2M1 x16: 0,8,16,24,32,48,64,96 both sides, 8 of 8. E4M3:
            ; all 128 magnitude codes identical, diff empty. Geometry 4194304 +
            ; 262144 = 4456448 both sides; scale byte 0x78 = 2^-7 both; the nibble
            ; order the cell flagged unproven confirmed, codes 12,10,4,5,2,10 on
            ; real bytes 0xAC,0x54,0xA2. And the constructions are unalike: ours is
            ; DERIVED (fd-value at eb 2, mb 1, the general IEEE decoder proven four
            ; ways for f16), ds4's is a hand table — which makes the agreement
            ; stronger than two ports of one algorithm would be.
            ; So: an oracle's job is to answer the same question independently, not
            ; to be the same KIND of thing as what it checks. Being right about why
            ; an option fails is not the same as having looked at all of them; the
            ; cheapest thing in the room was the one never costed.
            ; Still missing, plainly: no GENERATION oracle. ds4 cannot run this file
            ; (block addressing vs planar layout), so whole-model verdicts remain
            ; selfgauge. What changed is that the bottom of the stack — how bytes
            ; become numbers — is no longer self-witnessed, which matters given
            ; overfine 923: the cascade's most likely starting layer is now cleared.
            ; "askalike" — 0 hits before this row (peeroracle 0, smalloracle 0,
            ; narrowpeer 0).
