            ; 936 — exactwhere. The Q2_K MSL kernel's first device run disagreed
            ; with the CPU carver on 135 of 512 weights. The instinct is the kernel.
            ; The distribution said otherwise:
            ;   block0 (d = 0x3C00 = 1.0, dmin = 0x3800 = 0.5)     0 of 256 differ
            ;   block1 (d = 0x3555, dmin = 0xB400 NEGATIVE)      135 of 256 differ
            ;   max relative 4.616e-07, about four f32 ulps
            ; Every disagreement sits in the block whose constants are NOT exactly
            ; representable. The CPU carver runs Form's floats and the kernel runs
            ; f32: I had demanded that a lower-precision carrier reproduce a
            ; higher-precision one bit for bit. overfine 923 from the other side —
            ; there the REFERENCE was too precise to be faithful, here the GATE was.
            ; The easy repair is a tolerance everywhere, and it would have thrown
            ; away the 256 weights where exactness is real and free. So the claim
            ; was SPLIT where the evidence splits: block 0 exact equality demanded,
            ; block 1 f32's own granularity. Narrower than a blanket tolerance, not
            ; looser. And it has teeth — mutating the MSL to a contiguous stride
            ; fails 161 of 256 in BLOCK 0, and scaling the min per-element fails 186.
            ; A uniform tolerance would catch those only because they are large; a
            ; one-ulp fold error hides inside it and cannot hide from block 0.
            ; So: when two carriers disagree because they CARRY differently, find
            ; the sub-case where the property still holds exactly and keep it exact
            ; there — do not relax the whole claim to the weakest case. Strictness
            ; is not correctness: a gate can be wrong by asking for more than the
            ; world can give.
            ; The fixture made this available by accident — an awkward d and a
            ; negative dmin were put in block 1 to exercise the SIGN path, and that
            ; is what produced two blocks with different exactness properties. A
            ; fixture of convenient constants would have passed the wrong gate and
            ; taught nothing.
