            ; 944 — stridemush. Urs: "compressed how why". The HOW, from
            ; ds4.c:12326-12375: per layer with ratio r, a rolling buffer of the
            ; last r raw KVs plus a SCORE row each (compressor_kv/gate, ape bias);
            ; on the boundary, a per-dimension softmax over the r scores blends
            ; them into ONE row — score-gated, not mean, not max — then
            ; compressor_norm, comp_pos = pos+1-r, base-160000/scale-16 rope, fp8,
            ; into the SECOND cache. The WHY: train context is 1048576; raw f32 KV
            ; would be ~92 GB for 43 layers. Window raw + ratio-4/128 compressed +
            ; indexer top-512 makes 1M fit in a few GB.
            ; The row's own teaching is WHY THE GRAFT WAS FATAL rather than noisy.
            ; Since our lane rotated both q and k with the same wrong freqs,
            ; RELATIVE positions should survive — which is why it passed every
            ; gate. But scale_factor 16 divides positions by 16 before rotation.
            ; Compressed rows stand 4 or 128 apart: after /16 they still step by
            ; 0.25..8 — distinguishable. Raw tokens step by 1: phase steps of
            ; 1/16, fourteen tokens smeared inside one position's angle. The
            ; geometry is DESIGNED coarse; we fed it fine. Neighbors became
