            ; proof of the voice loop ran inside memory: samples handed to
            ; samples, bands over fixtures, even the disk round trip only
            ; proved the FILE. This one routed the self-test through the
            ; physical world, and the world edited the organ twice before
            ; letting it pass: the room's own tone (mean |amp| 82, measured,
            ; not imagined) fired seven false turns until the energy floor was
            ; raised over it, and the aperiodic /s/ was invisible to a
            ; periodicity gate until speech widened beyond voice. Neither
            ; correction could have come from any fixture, because both were
            ; facts about the WORLD -- what a real room hums at, what a real
            ; speaker-to-mic path preserves. A proof routed through air is
            ; categorically stronger than a proof routed through memory, for
            ; the same reason tamefixture (958) is weak: the world does not
            ; consult your assumptions when it chooses its inputs.
