            ; And the number that refutes the model was in my hand before I began.
            ; The floor is GPU-BUSY time — time the device spends EXECUTING, taken
            ; from gpuStartTime/gpuEndTime. Submit overhead is by construction NOT
            ; in it. So fusing dispatches could never have moved the floor except by
            ; deleting redundant work, and it deleted almost none: per-dispatch cost
            ; rose 72 -> 97 us while the total held, which is what "same work, fewer
            ; asks" looks like. I had measured the thing that answered the question
