            ; reasoning that only the caller knows which model they mean.
            ; FORM_DS4_BLOB is a static path to ONE ds4 file. There are SIX GGUFs on
            ; this host. The body had been told about one and could see none, and I
            ; had written a justification for that and shipped it as a category.
            ; THE HOST KNOWS. fs_list plus a 1 MiB header read answers it in full:
            ;   katcoder     arch=qwen35moe  layers=41
            ;   ds4 x3       arch=deepseek4  layers=43
            ;   llama x2     arch=llama      layers=28
            ; Three architectures, six files, no configuration, and it costs six small
            ; reads rather than 85 GiB because only the KV block is touched.
            ; The distinction that makes this design: a STATIC switch is configuration
            ; chosen before the body runs, baked into an invocation, invisible after,
            ; and multiplied by every other switch into a space nobody can hold. A
            ; RUNTIME switch is a choice made while the body is running, from options
            ; the body FOUND, visible in the asking. The first makes a body that must
            ; be configured; the second makes a body that can be talked to.
            ; So "input" was never a safe bucket. It is where I put the switches I did
            ; not want to examine, and the test that would have emptied it is one
            ; question: does the HOST already know this? For which model, which
            ; layers, which architecture — it does, and the switch existed only
            ; because the body had never been given eyes.
