            ; 1100 — valuedabsence. Chasing why a probe of mine answered a
            ; plausible 3, two siblings asked for coordinates and proposed a
            ; stale binary or call-position shadowing. Neither. Measured on
            ; fkwu:
            ;     (nothing? (str_byte_at "" 0))   = 0     it is NOT nothing
            ;     (str_byte_at "" 0)    eq (str_byte_at "abc" 3)   = 1
            ;     (str_byte_at "" 0)    eq (str_byte_at "abc" 99)  = 1
            ;     (str_byte_at "" 0)    eq -1                      = 1
            ;     (add (str_byte_at "" 0) 1)                       = 0
            ; The marker for "no byte here" is the ordinary integer -1. So it
            ; compares equal to the marker for "no byte THERE" — three distinct
            ; absences all equal — and it does arithmetic. My search loop
            ; compared a needle's first byte against each position's byte;
            ; one past the end BOTH sides were absent, absent equalled absent,
            ; and the loop reported a match at 3. Nothing refused. A position
            ; came out.
